{"id": "FRK-10", "kind": "math", "statement_nl": "Composite of the Fricke slash with itself is multiplication by the explicit scalar (-1)^k * N^(k-2): derived from W_N^2 = -N.I and Mathlib's slash normalisation |det g|^(k-1) * denom(g)^(-k), where for the scalar matrix c.I one has det = c^2 > 0 (so sigma = id), c.I acts trivially on H, and denom(c.I) = c. Consequently for even k the operator f |-> N^(1-k/2) * (f |[k] W_N) squares to the identity, giving the +1/-1 eigenspace decomposition. NOTE: the constant is N^(1-k/2) as a MULTIPLIER (equivalently divide by N^(k/2-1)); the earlier wording of this node did not fix the direction.", "lean_name": "SocrateAI.ModularForms.frickeW_sq_slash", "lean_file": "Lean/SocrateAI/ModularForms/FrickeComposite.lean", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["FRK-09", "FRK-02"], "paper_claim": null}
